# /etc/inittab -- busybox init (the kernel's PID 1 is /sbin/init -> busybox).
# This is Alpine's standard shape: openrc runs the three runlevels, one
# respawning getty per virtual terminal.  Indentation and the colon format
# are busybox's.
# openrc back on: the wedge (and the Xorg ppoll corruption) traced to a
# kernel slot-claim race -- two cores could fork into one 16 KiB kernel
# stack (proc.c g_slot_busy).  Timeout guards stay as a safety net.
::sysinit:/usr/bin/timeout 30 /sbin/openrc sysinit
::sysinit:/usr/bin/timeout 30 /sbin/openrc boot
::wait:/usr/bin/timeout 30 /sbin/openrc default
# The user-buffer probe regression test: a writev whose iovec runs off the
# image end must come back as an error, never a frozen machine (the shape
# that took a mount(8) stdio flush down; src/usr/bufoktest.c).
::wait:/bin/bufoktest.elf

# The Xfce desktop autostarts here, respawn-supervised like a display
# manager would: start-xfce runs the session in the foreground and init
# restarts the whole stack if it ever exits.
::respawn:/sbin/xfce-desktop

tty1::respawn:/sbin/agetty tty1
tty2::respawn:/sbin/agetty tty2
tty3::respawn:/sbin/agetty tty3
tty4::respawn:/sbin/agetty tty4
tty5::respawn:/sbin/agetty tty5
tty6::respawn:/sbin/agetty tty6

::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/sbin/openrc shutdown
